-- Final epic-arc briefings taken from the client localization
-- (missions whose wiki page has no MissionBriefing template).
-- +migrate Up
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='We need to get to the bottom of this. Those Amarr ships came from somewhere and someone. I can''t do the legwork myself. My MIO clearance can open a lot of doors, but there''s too much red tape for me to jump through. You, however, can do what I can''t. You can break this thing wide open. You need to talk to someone with both a knowledge of the Sansha and local connections. Luckily, I have just such a contact: Aralin Jick.' WHERE missionID=80101;
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I met again with Hyasyoda Agent Arikio Kuretsu after learning that Isha had discovered the location of the investigation team’s Headquarters. She told me that the CPF has a plan to deal with him personally, but for now I have been tasked with salvaging the situation. It seems that NOH have bugged the CPF compound, but we can use that against them. The strategy is to hack into their surveillance software, disable it, quickly evacuate everyone, and then clear the area before Hyasyoda agents detonate explosives laid inside. The explosions should register on the other bugging devices, and once each of them are destroyed, nobody will know that they were disabled a few moments beforehand, nor what happened in that small window of time after they were. At least, that’s the plan.' WHERE missionID=80124;
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Isha has somehow learned of the Hyasyoda investigation team and, worse yet, knows the location of their headquarters. He has asked me to level the place and destroy the mercenary ships guarding it. Hyasyoda assured me that any orders Isha gave over FTL comms would find their way back to the team, so I can only assume they’re aware of the matter. I should head back to Arikio Kuretsu at the Hyasyoda HQ to see how she wants to proceed.' WHERE missionID=80140;
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='We have to bring Katsen Isha down, and we have to be exceptionally careful about how we do it. Dealing with Nugoeihuvi requires cunning and guile. You''ve shown sound judgment by coming to us early, <Character>. The problem is that it will only get worse if you leave things as they are now. We need answers to the questions you''ve brought to light. We will count on you to earn Isha’s trust, so you can uncover whatever you need to help us. We need you on the inside if we’re ever going to see this resolved; Nugoeihuvi are too well trained at covering up their tracks. We will be there every step of the way to assist you. I’ve granted you provisional support from one of our best counter-intelligence teams. They will observe your actions from a distance and monitor any relevant data from your fluid router cache. Anything Isha says to you over FTL, we will have. Anything your camera drones see, we will see. You will have to keep your assignment strictly confidential, even from other Hyasyoda members. Nobody can know. Not your lover, not your mother, not even the Maker. If you need to get in touch, I will be here. Otherwise, act as if this conversation never happened.' WHERE missionID=80143;
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Though it was difficult, I made my choice. I decided to return Ralie to his father. I gotta say: The money was tempting. When I dropped Ralie off, we were ambushed by the Syndicate. I don’t know who tipped them off to our location, but I suspect a rat. Regardless, Ralie is safe with his father, and the Syndicate’s plot was disrupted. There’s bad blood in there somewhere, but where it comes from, I cannot say. All I know is that I saved a kid from a life of nightmares. Mission accomplished.' WHERE missionID=80168;
-- +migrate Down
-- (briefings stay)
